![high](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/high-priority.svg)

### Inefficient DOM Querying & Scroll-Spy Intersection Bug

There are two significant issues in this block:

1. **DOM Querying Performance:** `setActiveTocLink` is called frequently (on every intersection change during scrolling). Querying the DOM twice (`document.querySelectorAll`) on every call can cause layout thrashing and scroll stutter, especially on mobile devices. Caching the TOC links once after building the TOC avoids this overhead entirely.
2. **IntersectionObserver Logic Bug:** The `entries` parameter in the `IntersectionObserver` callback only contains elements whose intersection status *changed* in the current tick, not all currently intersecting elements. Sorting `entries` directly is highly unreliable because already-intersecting headings higher up will be missing from `entries`. This causes the active TOC link to get stuck or jump incorrectly when scrolling fast.

### Solution
- Cache the TOC links in a `tocLinks` array once.
- Maintain a persistent `Set` of currently intersecting heading IDs. On each tick, find the first heading in `tocTargets` (document order) that exists in the set to determine the active heading.

```javascript
    const tocLinks = Array.from(document.querySelectorAll('.docs-toc-link'));

    function setActiveTocLink(id) {
        if (!id) return;
        tocLinks.forEach((link) => {
            if (link.dataset.tocTarget === id) {
                link.classList.add('active');
                link.setAttribute('aria-current', 'location');
            } else if (link.classList.contains('active')) {
                link.classList.remove('active');
                link.removeAttribute('aria-current');
            }
        });
    }

    if ('IntersectionObserver' in window && tocTargets.length > 0) {
        const intersectingHeadings = new Set();
        const observer = new IntersectionObserver((entries) => {
            entries.forEach((entry) => {
                if (entry.isIntersecting) {
                    intersectingHeadings.add(entry.target.id);
                } else {
                    intersectingHeadings.delete(entry.target.id);
                }
            });
            const activeHeading = tocTargets.find((heading) => intersectingHeadings.has(heading.id));
            if (activeHeading) {
                setActiveTocLink(activeHeading.id);
            }
        }, { rootMargin: '-20% 0px -70% 0px', threshold: 0.01 });

        tocTargets.forEach((heading) => observer.observe(heading));
    }

    if (tocTargets[0]) {
        setActiveTocLink(tocTargets[0].id);
    }
```

